hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2726","Narrated to us Yunus, he said: Ibn Wahb informed us, that Malik informed him, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim ibn ‘Abdullah, that ‘Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Siddiq informed ‘Abdullah ibn ‘Umar, from ‘A’ishah (RA), that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:\n\n“Have you not seen what your people did when they rebuilt the Ka‘bah? They shortened it from the foundations of Ibrahim (AS).”\n\nShe said: “O Messenger of Allah, why did you not restore it to the foundations of Ibrahim (AS)?”\n\nHe (ﷺ) said: “Were it not for the recent unbelief of your people.”\n\nIbn ‘Umar (RA) said: “If ‘A’ishah (RA) had heard this from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), I do not think the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would have left touching the two corners that are adjacent to the Black Stone, except that the House had not been built upon the foundations of Ibrahim (AS).”\n\n---\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
